@startuml custom-app-launch-workflow
title Custom SMART on FHIR Application Launch & Execution Workflow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 8

actor "Developer /\nClinician" as User
participant "FHIR Studio UI\n(EHR Simulator)" as UI
participant "Custom SMART App\n(Web / Client)" as App
participant "SMART IdP\n(FHIR Studio Server)" as IdP
participant "FHIR Gateway\n(FHIR Studio Server)" as Gateway
database "HAPI FHIR JPA\n(Partitioned)" as HAPI

== 1. App Registration & Sandbox Preparation ==

User -> UI : Register Custom App\n(Client ID, Launch URI, Redirect URIs, Scopes, Auth Method)
UI -> IdP : Create/Update App record
IdP --> UI : App Registered

User -> UI : Select Sandbox, Target Patient & User Persona
UI -> UI : Configure Launch Scenario / Context

== 2. SMART EHR Launch Initiation ==

User -> UI : Launch Application (via EHR Simulator or Scenario)
UI -> IdP : POST /api/sandboxes/{id}/launch-context\n{patientFhirId, userPersonaId, encounterFhirId, appId, fhirContext}
activate IdP
IdP -> IdP : Generate unique launchId\nStore pending context in DB (15 min TTL)
IdP --> UI : 201 Created { launch: "uuid", sandboxId: "id" }
deactivate IdP

UI -> App : Load launch_uri in Simulator Iframe\n?launch={launchId}&iss={fhirBaseUrl}
activate App

== 3. SMART Authorization (OAuth2 + PKCE) ==

App -> App : Generate PKCE code_verifier\nand code_challenge (S256)
App -> IdP : GET /oauth/authorize\n?response_type=code&client_id={clientId}\n&redirect_uri={redirectUri}&scope={scopes}\n&launch={launchId}&code_challenge={challenge}&state={state}
activate IdP

IdP -> IdP : Validate client & redirect_uri\nResolve launch context (patient, persona, sandbox)\nVerify user authorization / persona context
IdP -> IdP : Generate authorization code\nBind PKCE challenge & session context
IdP --> App : 302 Redirect to {redirectUri}?code={authCode}&state={state}
deactivate IdP

== 4. Token Exchange ==

App -> IdP : POST /oauth/token\n(grant_type=authorization_code, code={authCode},\nredirect_uri={redirectUri}, client_id={clientId},\ncode_verifier={verifier} / client_secret / client_assertion)
activate IdP

IdP -> IdP : Verify authorization code & code_verifier (PKCE)\nValidate client credentials / JWT signature
IdP -> IdP : Mint signed access_token (JWT / opaque)\nGenerate id_token & SMART launch context
IdP --> App : 200 OK\n{\n  "access_token": "...",\n  "token_type": "Bearer",\n  "expires_in": 3600,\n  "scope": "...",\n  "patient": "{patientId}",\n  "need_patient_banner": true,\n  "smart_style_url": "...",\n  "id_token": "..."\n}
deactivate IdP

== 5. FHIR Resource Data Access ==

App -> Gateway : GET /api/sandboxes/{id}/fhir/R4/Patient/{patientId}\nAuthorization: Bearer {access_token}
activate Gateway

Gateway -> Gateway : Verify access_token signature & expiry\nValidate SMART scope permissions (e.g. patient/*.rs)\nResolve Sandbox partition ID
Gateway -> HAPI : GET /fhir/Patient/{patientId}\nTenant-Identification: Partition-ID {partitionId}
activate HAPI
HAPI --> Gateway : FHIR Patient Resource (JSON)
deactivate HAPI

Gateway -> Gateway : Rewrite absolute bundle / server URLs to Gateway base URL
Gateway --> App : 200 OK FHIR Patient JSON
deactivate Gateway

App -> Gateway : GET /api/sandboxes/{id}/fhir/R4/Observation?patient={patientId}\nAuthorization: Bearer {access_token}
activate Gateway
Gateway -> HAPI : Query Observation resources (Partition ID)
activate HAPI
HAPI --> Gateway : Observation Searchset Bundle
deactivate HAPI
Gateway --> App : 200 OK FHIR Observation Bundle
deactivate Gateway

App -> App : Render clinical data in UI / EHR Simulator

deactivate App

@enduml
